        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cooperating Processes",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Independent process cannot affect or be affected by the execution of another process",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Cooperating process can affect or be affected by the execution of another process",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Advantages of process cooperation",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Information sharing",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Computation speed-up",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Modularity",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Convenience",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 4,
      "title": "Producer-Consumer Problem",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Producer-Consumer Problem",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Paradigm for cooperating processes, producer process produces information that is consumed by a consumer process",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "unbounded-buffer places no practical limit on the size of the buffer",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "bounded-buffer assumes that there is a fixed buffer size",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 5,
      "title": "Bounded-Buffer – Shared-Memory Solution",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bounded-Buffer – Shared-Memory Solution",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Shared data",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "#define BUFFER_SIZE 10\nTypedef struct {",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": ". . .",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "} item;\nitem buffer[BUFFER_SIZE];\nint in = 0;\nint out = 0;",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Solution is correct, but can only use BUFFER_SIZE-1 elements",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 6,
      "title": "Bounded-Buffer – Insert() Method",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bounded-Buffer – Insert() Method",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "    while (true) {\n   /* Produce an item */\n       while((((in + 1) % BUFFER SIZE count)  == out)\n        // ;   /* do nothing -- no free buffers */",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Busy waiting",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "        buffer[in] = item;\n        in = (in + 1) % BUFFER SIZE;\n}",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 7,
      "title": "Bounded Buffer – Remove() Method",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bounded Buffer – Remove() Method",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "    while (true) {\n          while (in == out)\n                 ; // do nothing -- nothing to consume\n         // remove an item from the buffer\n         item = buffer[out];\n         out = (out + 1) % BUFFER SIZE;\n    return item;\n     }",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 8,
      "title": "Background",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Background",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Concurrent access to shared data may result in data inconsistency",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Maintaining data consistency requires mechanisms to ensure the orderly execution of cooperating processes",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Suppose that we wanted to provide a solution to the consumer-producer problem that fills all the buffers. We can do so by having an integer count that keeps track of the number of full buffers. Initially, count is set to 0. It is incremented by the producer after it produces a new buffer and is decremented by the consumer after it consumes a buffer.",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 9,
      "title": "Producer",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Producer",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "while (true) {\n          /*  produce an item and put in nextProduced  */\n          while (count == BUFFER_SIZE)\n            ; // do nothing\n               buffer [in] = nextProduced;\n               in = (in + 1) % BUFFER_SIZE;\n               count++;\n}",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 10,
      "title": "Consumer",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Consumer",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "    while (true)  {\n            while (count == 0)\n                ; // do nothing\n                nextConsumed =  buffer[out];\n                 out = (out + 1) % BUFFER_SIZE;\n                      count--;\n            /*  consume the item in nextConsumed\n    }",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 11,
      "title": "Race Condition",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Race Condition",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "count++ could be implemented as\n\n register1 = count\n register1 = register1 + 1\n count = register1",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "count-- could be implemented as\n\n register2 = count\n register2 = register2 - 1\n count = register2",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Consider this execution interleaving with “count = 5” initially:",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "S0: producer execute register1 = count {register1 = 5}\nS1: producer execute register1 = register1 + 1 {register1 = 6} \nS2: consumer execute register2 = count {register2 = 5} \nS3: consumer execute register2 = register2 - 1 {register2 = 4} \nS4: producer execute count = register1 {count = 6 } \nS5: consumer execute count = register2 {count = 4}",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 12,
      "title": "PROCESS SYNCHRONIZATION",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "PROCESS SYNCHRONIZATION",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "A section of code, common to n cooperating processes, in which the processes may be accessing common variables.",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "A Critical Section Environment contains:",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Entry Section Code requesting entry into the critical section.",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Critical Section Code in which only one process can execute at any one time.",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Exit Section The end of the critical section, releasing or allowing others in.",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Remainder Section Rest of the code AFTER the critical section.",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Critical Sections",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 13,
      "title": "Solution to Critical-Section Problem",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Solution to Critical-Section Problem",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "1. Mutual Exclusion - If process Pi is executing in its critical section, then no other processes can be executing in their critical sections",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "2. Progress - If no process is executing in its critical section and there exist some processes that wish to enter their critical section, then the selection of the processes that will enter the critical section next cannot be postponed indefinitely",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "3. Bounded Waiting - A bound must exist on the number of times that other processes are allowed to enter their critical sections after a process has made a request to enter its critical section and before that request is granted.",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 14,
      "title": "Peterson’s Solution",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Peterson’s Solution",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Two process solution",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Assume that the LOAD and STORE instructions are atomic; that is, cannot be interrupted.",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "The two processes share two variables:",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "int turn;",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Boolean flag[2]",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "The variable turn indicates whose turn it is to enter the critical section.",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "The flag array is used to indicate if a process is ready to enter the critical section. flag[i] = true implies that process Pi is ready!",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "slide",
      "number": 15,
      "title": "Algorithm for Process Pi",
      "images": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Algorithm for Process Pi",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "    while (true) {\n               flag[i] = TRUE;\n               turn = j;\n               while ( flag[j] == true && turn == j);",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "CRITICAL SECTION",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "               flag[i] = FALSE;",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "REMAINDER SECTION",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "       }",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
